WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:03.140
- On this episode, I talk
about my favorite sneakers,

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.438
how I hustled a decade ago,

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.592
and VaynerMedia's holiday party.

00:00:11.732 --> 00:00:14.685
You ask questions and I answer them.

00:00:14.685 --> 00:00:16.318
(intro music)

00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:19.840
This is the #AskGaryVee Show.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.551
(intro music)

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:28.697
Hey everybody, this is Gary Vay-ner-chuk

00:00:28.697 --> 00:00:30.299
and welcome to episode 52

00:00:30.299 --> 00:00:32.644
of the #AskGaryVee Show.

00:00:32.644 --> 00:00:35.453
Big day today here at VaynerMedia.

00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:37.009
It is the holiday party.

00:00:37.009 --> 00:00:39.656
I don't know who decided
to make this a Wednesday.

00:00:39.656 --> 00:00:40.329
- [Steve] Thank you.

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:42.072
- Right? I mean...

00:00:43.394 --> 00:00:45.113
Are you guys pumped for the holiday party?

00:00:45.113 --> 00:00:47.226
- [in unison] Yeah!

00:00:47.226 --> 00:00:48.990
- Thursday's gonna be a disaster.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.058
(laughter)

00:00:50.058 --> 00:00:51.825
Let's get into the show.

00:00:51.825 --> 00:00:53.680
- [Voiceover] Harvest Funders asks

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.677
what does hustle look like for you now

00:00:55.677 --> 00:00:58.162
versus five or even 10 years ago?

00:00:58.162 --> 00:00:59.860
Why has it changed?

00:01:01.157 --> 00:01:03.177
- This is such a great question.

00:01:03.177 --> 00:01:04.849
Thanks Harvest for it.

00:01:04.849 --> 00:01:06.219
And I'm gonna expand on it.

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:08.239
I'm gonna long form on,

00:01:08.239 --> 00:01:11.536
I was even talking to DRock and Staphon

00:01:11.536 --> 00:01:12.465
that this might have to turn into

00:01:12.465 --> 00:01:14.670
a three to five minute video movie

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.108
because I'm starting to
have this weird realization.

00:01:17.108 --> 00:01:20.278
I've been talking to Mike, Trainer Mike,

00:01:20.278 --> 00:01:21.636
about this during the workouts

00:01:21.636 --> 00:01:23.819
which is like, wait a minute.

00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:26.976
Was I really hustling at 25 to 30?

00:01:26.976 --> 00:01:28.788
I wasn't into email culture yet

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:32.162
nor was the wine industry nor was society.

00:01:32.162 --> 00:01:34.058
The store closed at nine.

00:01:34.058 --> 00:01:36.427
You know, after a while 7:30 felt like

00:01:36.427 --> 00:01:37.936
the appropriate time to leave.

00:01:37.936 --> 00:01:39.747
You know, I had girlfriends
that I lived with.

00:01:39.747 --> 00:01:41.659
Brandon, my best friend
who runs Wine Library

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:42.882
lived above me.

00:01:42.882 --> 00:01:45.598
And like, you know, I can
sit here and think about,

00:01:45.598 --> 00:01:48.640
you know, 8:30 at night
on a Wednesday at 26

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.426
playing like Monopoly on GameCube

00:01:51.426 --> 00:01:55.586
and that is just not even remotely close

00:01:55.586 --> 00:01:56.859
in the equation at this point.

00:01:56.859 --> 00:01:59.065
You know, it's really
fun to be a businessman

00:01:59.065 --> 00:02:01.573
instead of an athlete because your prime

00:02:01.573 --> 00:02:04.800
is so much further down the path

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.099
and you have so much
more time to get there.

00:02:07.099 --> 00:02:09.383
Wait no, look athletes,
a lot of those people,

00:02:09.383 --> 00:02:11.636
those kids are, you know, hustling

00:02:11.636 --> 00:02:13.400
in Junior High and High School and so

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.814
maybe the timing's a
little bit different but,

00:02:15.814 --> 00:02:17.998
you know, the truth is my hustle today

00:02:17.998 --> 00:02:20.645
is at an all-time high
especially since June 7th

00:02:20.645 --> 00:02:22.455
when I've incorporated working out

00:02:22.455 --> 00:02:26.217
which has driven me to
wake up so much earlier.

00:02:26.217 --> 00:02:29.328
Not that I have more energy
'cause I was high on sugar,

00:02:29.328 --> 00:02:31.305
I've come to realize but,

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:33.624
I can tell you this.

00:02:33.624 --> 00:02:34.878
Let's start with this.

00:02:34.878 --> 00:02:36.945
Every person right here in this circle,

00:02:36.945 --> 00:02:38.174
this inner circle of five

00:02:38.174 --> 00:02:41.124
and anybody out there that really knows

00:02:41.124 --> 00:02:42.076
and some of you have watched

00:02:42.076 --> 00:02:44.467
and I've thrown up my
calendar here and there,

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:48.183
nobody comes close to me and really sniffs

00:02:48.183 --> 00:02:51.451
my level of hustle and
how much work I put in

00:02:51.451 --> 00:02:54.823
and don't take a step
back in saying, really?

00:02:54.823 --> 00:02:57.772
Because it is literally
every second of every minute

00:02:57.772 --> 00:03:00.372
of every day for a very
long period of time

00:03:00.372 --> 00:03:03.368
and you hear about it,
Alex heard about it.

00:03:03.368 --> 00:03:04.365
He was a fan.

00:03:04.365 --> 00:03:06.642
He knew what I was spitting
through this, right.

00:03:06.642 --> 00:03:07.919
He worked at VaynerMedia

00:03:07.919 --> 00:03:11.749
but until he got a little
closer, it gets really intense.

00:03:11.749 --> 00:03:15.233
It gets intense when I'm
working the way I'm working

00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:18.831
and I'm texting 17 times on a
Saturday while I'm in the air

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.991
and saying do this, do
this and this, and this.

00:03:20.991 --> 00:03:23.729
I'm gonna do this and
this and this and this

00:03:23.729 --> 00:03:25.960
and this and this.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:29.144
And so, my hustle is up.

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:31.788
- [Voiceover] Lyndon asks

00:03:31.788 --> 00:03:34.226
in the first 30 seconds
of someone meeting you,

00:03:34.226 --> 00:03:35.979
what do you reveal about yourself?

00:03:37.289 --> 00:03:38.661
- Lyndon, this is a great question

00:03:38.661 --> 00:03:39.868
and I'm gonna give you a great,

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:42.608
I'm declaring a great answer alert.

00:03:42.608 --> 00:03:45.394
(trumpets blaring)

00:03:49.054 --> 00:03:52.554
I can probably get somebody to

00:03:52.554 --> 00:03:55.759
consume something from me
within the first 13 seconds

00:03:55.759 --> 00:03:58.940
let alone 30 seconds because
it's not what I'm gonna say,

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.101
it's how I feel.

00:04:00.101 --> 00:04:04.025
See, words are great but
energy's a whole different game

00:04:04.025 --> 00:04:05.743
and I win on that game, right.

00:04:05.743 --> 00:04:07.230
And so within the first 30 seconds,

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.760
I'm gonna establish and
have always established

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.708
from my entire life from first grade,

00:04:13.708 --> 00:04:16.702
first 30 seconds in to
any business meeting

00:04:16.702 --> 00:04:18.166
to when I'm in a big off site

00:04:18.166 --> 00:04:19.442
when everybody goes around the room

00:04:19.442 --> 00:04:21.324
and says, "I'm Staphon.
I work at VaynerMedia."

00:04:21.324 --> 00:04:23.808
But then I do my, "I'm
Gary, I'm a Jets fan."

00:04:23.808 --> 00:04:27.337
Like, I within 30 seconds, set the tone

00:04:27.337 --> 00:04:29.427
vibe wise, if I don't get to say something

00:04:29.427 --> 00:04:30.912
which is rare for me, not to say something

00:04:30.912 --> 00:04:33.072
within the first 30 seconds.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:36.323
I establish that I'm different.

00:04:36.323 --> 00:04:37.693
Yeah, I'm different.

00:04:38.723 --> 00:04:41.431
- [Voiceover] YaboyLV asks
what is your favorite pair

00:04:41.431 --> 00:04:43.869
of sneakers of all time?

00:04:43.869 --> 00:04:46.284
- That's a nice little segue
from the last question.

00:04:46.284 --> 00:04:49.186
My favorite pair of sneakers hands down

00:04:49.186 --> 00:04:53.644
is the 1985, I think,
Patrick Ewing Adidas.

00:04:53.644 --> 00:04:54.805
I'm a huge Knicks fan.

00:04:54.805 --> 00:04:58.195
Let me tell you my all-time
hated pairs of shoes.

00:04:58.195 --> 00:05:00.982
Every single Air Jordans of all time

00:05:00.982 --> 00:05:03.280
because I hate Michael Jordan.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.320
And I love Patrick
Ewing and the 85 Adidas.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.015
- [Voiceover] Mike asks, I've caught a few

00:05:09.015 --> 00:05:12.104
of your #AskGaryVee shows
and love the content.

00:05:12.104 --> 00:05:13.984
What are your thoughts on Google+?

00:05:13.984 --> 00:05:16.329
Why do you continue to use it?

00:05:16.329 --> 00:05:18.837
- Mike, I think Google+
is a failure for Google.

00:05:18.837 --> 00:05:21.345
Once again, a big company that is amazing,

00:05:21.345 --> 00:05:25.965
maybe, actually, my pick
for the best company

00:05:25.965 --> 00:05:28.449
in tech in the world.

00:05:28.449 --> 00:05:31.078
But, just doing something
outside of their DNA.

00:05:32.399 --> 00:05:34.162
They try to copy something.

00:05:34.162 --> 00:05:37.134
It was ill-fated in my opinion.

00:05:37.134 --> 00:05:39.711
I still use it because there's
an audience of mine there.

00:05:39.711 --> 00:05:43.263
It ties in nicely to the YouTube society.

00:05:43.263 --> 00:05:45.400
There's a small niche group of people

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.116
that I massively respect from Google+

00:05:48.116 --> 00:05:50.577
that are early adopters of technology,

00:05:50.577 --> 00:05:53.364
early Twitter users and they've
created a nice community.

00:05:53.364 --> 00:05:57.769
And much like every social
network besides Twitter,

00:05:57.769 --> 00:06:00.463
most social networks are not so social.

00:06:00.463 --> 00:06:03.412
They're content distribution
portals, unfortunately.

00:06:03.412 --> 00:06:06.383
And I've got some audience there

00:06:06.383 --> 00:06:08.056
and I will continue to
distribute my content

00:06:08.056 --> 00:06:10.656
considering that it's so
native to the YouTube platform

00:06:10.656 --> 00:06:12.235
where so much of this goes.

00:06:12.235 --> 00:06:14.372
I mean, obviously people
listening on the podcast know.

00:06:14.372 --> 00:06:15.346
I was talking to a bunch of people

00:06:15.346 --> 00:06:16.623
that are listening to the podcast.

00:06:16.623 --> 00:06:18.457
Hey podcast peeps, you know,

00:06:18.457 --> 00:06:20.507
that how sometimes they go and run

00:06:20.507 --> 00:06:21.250
and watch the show.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.641
As a matter of fact, one of
our VaynerMedia employees

00:06:23.641 --> 00:06:25.986
heard me say Asia and something else

00:06:25.986 --> 00:06:28.842
and thought that I called you Asia

00:06:28.842 --> 00:06:30.328
because they thought
that I was thinking India

00:06:30.328 --> 00:06:32.418
and I said Asia and then
I punched them in the face

00:06:32.418 --> 00:06:34.856
and said, "Do you really
think I wouldn't know that?"

00:06:34.856 --> 00:06:39.856
Anyway, so they wanna watch
the video is my point.

00:06:40.397 --> 00:06:43.238
My big point is, what I think about it is,

00:06:43.238 --> 00:06:46.141
it's a loss but it still has value

00:06:46.141 --> 00:06:47.092
and that's something that I want

00:06:47.092 --> 00:06:49.205
everybody to pay attention to.

00:06:49.205 --> 00:06:51.207
Nothing is ever dead.

00:06:51.207 --> 00:06:53.362
I talk about email open rates being down

00:06:53.362 --> 00:06:56.566
but email's probably at the
top of my marketing strategy.

00:06:56.566 --> 00:07:00.513
It's not about 100 or
zero, it's where is it

00:07:00.513 --> 00:07:02.371
at this moment.

00:07:02.371 --> 00:07:04.391
And where Google+ is at this moment

00:07:04.391 --> 00:07:07.200
is it still merits the
minimal time it takes

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.615
for me to post a YouTube
video on that platform

00:07:09.615 --> 00:07:11.669
and occasionally engage
with that community.

00:07:11.669 --> 00:07:15.002
Something that MySpace
no longer brings to me

00:07:15.002 --> 00:07:18.649
but did in 2009 and 10
with Wine Library TV.

00:07:18.649 --> 00:07:20.128
Get it?

00:07:20.128 --> 00:07:22.084
- [Voiceover] Simplybeingmum asks,

00:07:22.084 --> 00:07:24.266
are you a morning person?

00:07:24.266 --> 00:07:25.946
- I am not a morning person.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.654
I sleep like a brick.

00:07:29.654 --> 00:07:33.205
Like, I mean, I literally believe that

00:07:33.205 --> 00:07:35.086
somebody could break into my home,

00:07:35.086 --> 00:07:37.385
stab me in the leg with a knife

00:07:37.385 --> 00:07:39.428
and still then continue
to steal everything

00:07:39.428 --> 00:07:40.956
out of my apartment.

00:07:40.956 --> 00:07:42.447
I just sleep hard.

00:07:42.447 --> 00:07:45.094
And so when I wake up,
it's just not great.

00:07:45.094 --> 00:07:48.019
That being said, no
question, I'm waking up

00:07:48.019 --> 00:07:50.162
a hell of a lot better
because of my working out.

00:07:50.162 --> 00:07:51.711
A lot of times I've been talking about

00:07:51.711 --> 00:07:53.034
how I haven't picked up energy

00:07:53.034 --> 00:07:55.960
but what I have picked up
is the ability to wake up

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.212
on this five and half,
six hour kind of window

00:07:58.212 --> 00:07:59.791
that I sleep, which I
know a lot of you think

00:07:59.791 --> 00:08:01.068
I sleep three or four hours.

00:08:01.068 --> 00:08:02.577
Heck, I'd sleep seven or eight

00:08:02.577 --> 00:08:05.089
if I can really like, when and if I can...

00:08:05.089 --> 00:08:06.873
By the way, and this is a
whole another long thing

00:08:06.873 --> 00:08:08.754
that we gotta get into eventually,

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:10.333
it's not about how much you sleep.

00:08:10.333 --> 00:08:13.421
It's what you do while you're awake.

00:08:13.421 --> 00:08:16.512
So, a couple things for
the question of the day.

00:08:16.512 --> 00:08:20.015
Obviously today is
VaynerMedia's holiday party.

00:08:20.015 --> 00:08:22.267
Please tell me in the
question of the day, a story.

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:23.173
It's not a question.

00:08:23.173 --> 00:08:24.868
It's story time, VaynerNation.

00:08:24.868 --> 00:08:28.296
Tell me your most interesting story

00:08:28.296 --> 00:08:31.671
from a corporate or company holiday party.

00:08:31.671 --> 00:08:33.668
I need a little gossip in my life.

00:08:33.668 --> 00:08:36.058
And number two, why
are you not visiting me

00:08:36.058 --> 00:08:38.907
at the Wine Library on Saturday?

00:08:38.907 --> 00:08:41.548
You keep asking questions.

00:08:41.548 --> 00:08:45.126
I, get it, will keep answering them.

00:08:45.126 --> 00:08:47.971
Don't forget to subscribe
to my YouTube channel.

00:08:47.971 --> 00:08:52.971
(hip hop music)

